# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform — local artifact hygiene.
#
# This file exists so the infra foundation never leaks state, plugins or real
# values into Git. The Terraform state stores secrets in PLAINTEXT even when an
# output is marked `sensitive`, so it is never committed.
#
# What does NOT go here, and why:
#   - *.tf              → the infrastructure itself, committed on purpose
#   - .terraform.lock.hcl → pins the resolved provider versions
#   - terraform.tfvars.example → value contract, safe and committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Plugins and modules downloaded by `terraform init`.
.terraform/
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info

# Local state. `.backup` files and copies are just as dangerous.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup

# Provider crash logs (credentials may show up in the stack trace).
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Real account values: may contain account identifiers and region.
*.auto.tfvars
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars.json
terraform.tfvars.json

# Local overrides break the state precisely because they are not committed.
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Local CLI/credential config and hand-made backend config.
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
backend.hcl

# Saved plans may contain output values in readable text.
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.*

# Kubeconfig copied from the VM: ignored in the root .gitignore, which covers
# the whole repository.
